@cc [owner:spolu,notify:spolu,label:architecture;error-handling] storage-transport-independence
Storage and resource modules MUST return transport-independent errors and MUST NOT import tonic or
construct gRPC statuses. Conversions to API statuses MUST live in the API layer.

@cc [owner:spolu,notify:spolu,label:backend;error-handling] strongly-typed-resource-errors
Resource domain errors MUST use an Error enum defined in the resource module, with distinct variants
for failures callers need to distinguish. They MUST be returned through Result, directly or wrapped
in storage::Error<Error>, and MUST NOT be reduced to strings or anyhow::Error. Callers MUST match
variants instead of parsing error messages. Database and stored-data decoding failures MAY propagate
as FdbBindingError.

@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:backend;error-handling] retry-safe-resource-writes
Resource methods that write FDB MUST be safe to run again, with the same inputs, in a new transaction
after an attempt that committed with an unknown result. The re-run MUST succeed and leave state
equivalent to a single run, recognizing its own commit from IDs, keys or hashes created before the
transaction. `SessionResource::refresh` MAY extend expiry again. Exceptions: `SessionResource::revoke`
returns NotFound when it finds the session it revoked, and `SessionResource::revoke_expired` MAY
clean up a further batch.

@cc [owner:pmilliotte,label:testing] resource-write-retry-tests
Each resource method that writes FDB, except the exceptions above, MUST have a test that commits it,
runs it again in a new transaction, and checks that the re-run succeeds and leaves stored state
unchanged, or equivalent where the method allows it.
